From ff5e0dc71bee860a5e689b511ad7f7c3a8408604 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 21:27:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] shell: Restart the UI from the power menu and the system menu

Offer "Restart UI" in the power menu (long press on the power button,
right of "Power Off"; "Restart", "Lock", "Screenshot" and the emergency
button follow in reading order, all six as large as each other) and in
the system menu of the quick settings. It fades out and quits the shell
with a failure status, so that the systemd user unit
(Restart=on-failure) starts it again. The compositor and the running
apps stay. The new shell starts locked, as at every start without a
display manager. Not offered on the lock screen.

The system menu no longer has a fixed width with labels cut in the
middle: it takes the width of its longest entry.

Translations for de, es, fr, it, nl, pl, pt, pt_BR and ru.
